      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a gritty, street-level urban crime drama, consider casting characters with authentic backgrounds and vibes. For detectives, you might have:\n\n* A veteran, worn-down detective from a broken home with a troubled past, serving as a mentor to newer, more idealistic detectives.\n* A by-the-book, unhurried detective from a diverse neighborhood with a deep understanding of the community and street dynamics.\n* A rebellious, rule-breaking detective who often clashes with departmental standards, giving the show an edgy, refreshing perspective.\n\nFor gang members, consider diversity in your casting and backgrounds, such as:\n\n* A young, ambitious gang leader from a low-income neighborhood with a strong sense of loyalty and desperation.\n* A high-ranking member of a well-established gang with deep roots in the city, embodying an old-school, hardcore persona.\n* A disillusioned, weary gang member who is questioning the organization and its purpose, serving as a potential anti-hero.\n\nTo add authenticity, focus on casting actors from the same ethnic backgrounds as your intended audience.",
